   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "פֵּירְשׁוּ לֹא יַעֲלוּ [וְכוּ׳]. אָמַר רַבִּי זֵירָא: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא שֶׁפֵּירְשׁוּ כְּלַפֵּי מַטָּה, אֲבָל כְּלַפֵּי מַעְלָה – קָרוֹבֵי הוּא דְּאַקְרִיבוּ לְעִיכּוּל. וַאֲפִילּוּ פֵּירְשׁוּ?!",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that items that are not meant for consumption on the altar, such as the bones and tendons, are sacrificed along with the flesh if they are attached to it. But if «they separated they shall not ascend. Rabbi Zeira said:» The Sages «taught» that if they separated from the flesh they shall not ascend «only when they separated» from the offering «downward,» i.e., away from the altar, whereby they became distanced from the pyre when they were separated. «But» if they separated from the offering «upward,» i.e., they became closer to the pyre when they were separated from the offering, «they have become closer to consumption» and shall ascend. The Gemara asks: «And even» if «they separated,» shall they be offered? Doesn’t the mishna state that they shall ascend only if they are still attached to the flesh?"
  }
 ],
